# Tabs

Alternatives for the same step. Each `tab` has a `title`. Tabs that share a `sync` name follow
each other, and the choice is remembered in the browser. Without scripts every tab is shown.

`````markdown
::::tabs sync="system"
:::tab title="Linux"
Run `sh install.sh`.
:::
:::tab title="Windows"
Run `install.ps1`.
:::
::::
`````

::::tabs sync="system"
:::tab title="Linux"
Run `sh install.sh`.
:::
:::tab title="Windows"
Run `install.ps1`.
:::
::::

A second group with the same `sync` name switches along with the first:

::::tabs sync="system"
:::tab title="Linux"
Open a terminal.
:::
:::tab title="Windows"
Open a terminal in the folder.
:::
::::
